  "answer": "**Changed:** `normalize.mjs` — `normalizeText` now collapses every nonempty run of internal whitespace to a single ASCII space via `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` between `trim()` and `toLowerCase()`. Export name, signature, and `TypeError` behavior are unchanged.\n\n**Behavior notes:**\n- `trim()` removes leading/trailing JS whitespace; `\\s` in JS regex matches the same whitespace set (space, tab, line breaks, form feed, vertical tab, NBSP, Unicode space separators), so internal runs of those become one `' '`.\n- Empty/whitespace-only input → `''` (trim yields `''`, replace is a no-op).\n- Lowercasing uses `String.prototype.toLowerCase()` as required.\n\n**Checked:** only the file contents were read and rewritten; no tests were executed (no shell/test tool available), so I can't claim the public tests pass.",
